 "text": "Global Context Environmental Indicators Ireland 2021 - Central Statistics Office\n\n# Environmental Indicators Ireland 2021 \n\n## 1.1 World: Population 1950-2020\n\n 1.1 World: Population 1950-2020 \n\n| Table 1.1 World: Population 1950-2020 | | | | | | | | | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| % of world population | | | | | | | | | Population (millions) |\n| Year | Africa | Asia | Caribbean | Central America | Europe | North America | Oceania | South America | World |\n| 1950 | 9% | 55% | 1% | 1% | 22% | 7% | 1% | 4% | 2,536 |\n| 1960 | 9% | 56% | 1% | 2% | 20% | 7% | 1% | 5% | 3,035 |\n| 1970 | 10% | 58% | 1% | 2% | 18% | 6% | 1% | 5% | 3,700 |\n| 1980 | 11% | 59% | 1% | 2% | 16% | 6% | 1% | 5% | 4,458 |\n| 1990 | 12% | 61% | 1% | 2% | 14% | 5% | 1% | 6% | 5,327 |\n| 2000 | 13% | 61% | 1% | 2% | 12% | 5% | 1% | 6% | 6,143 |\n| 2010 | 15% | 61% | 1% | 2% | 11% | 5% | 1% | 6% | 6,957 |\n| 2015 | 16% | 60% | 1% | 2% | 10% | 5% | 1% | 6% | 7,380 |\n| 2016 | 16% | 60% | 1% | 2% | 10% | 5% | 1% | 6% | 7,464 |\n| 2017 | 16% | 60% | 1% | 2% | 10% | 5% | 1% | 6% | 7,548 |\n| 2018 | 17% | 60% | 1% | 2% | 10% | 5% | 1% | 6% | 7,631 |\n| 2019 | 17% | 60% | 1% | 2% | 10% | 5% | 1% | 6% | 7,713 |\n| 2020 | 17% | 60% | 1% | 2% | 10% | 5% | 1% | 6% | 7,795 |\n| Source: United Nations | | | | | | | | | |\n\nOpen in Excel: Environmental Indicators Ireland 2021 Table 1.1 (XLS 12KB) \n\nGlobal population increased by 207% from 2.5 billion to 7.8 billion between 1950 and 2020.\n\nAfrica‘s share of the World’s population increased from 9% in 1950 to 17% in 2020, while Europe’s fell from 22% to 10% over the same period. In 2020, Asia was the World region with the largest share of the World’s population at 60%.\n\n## 1.2 World: Child mortality rates 1950-2020\n\n 1.2 World: Child mortality rates 1950-2020 \n\n| Table 1.2 World: Child mortality rates 1950-2020 | | | | | | | | | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Deaths before age five per 1,000 live births | | | | | | | | | |\n| Year | Africa | Asia | Caribbean | Central America | Europe | North America | Oceania | South America | World |\n| 1950-1955 | 311 | 234 | 184 | 204 | 93 | 36 | 94 | 180 | 213 |\n| 1955-1960 | 283 | 217 | 160 | 173 | 62 | 32 | 79 | 163 | 193 |\n| 1960-1965 | 259 | 205 | 136 | 149 | 44 | 29 | 69 | 145 | 182 |\n| 1965-1970 | 239 | 167 | 119 | 131 | 35 | 26 | 60 | 128 | 156 |\n| 1970-1975 | 220 | 144 | 103 | 111 | 29 | 21 | 53 | 110 | 138 |\n| 1975-1980 | 200 | 127 | 93 | 88 | 26 | 17 | 49 | 94 | 124 |\n| 1980-1985 | 182 | 109 | 85 | 71 | 22 | 13 | 43 | 77 | 109 |\n| 1985-1990 | 170 | 93 | 73 | 57 | 19 | 12 | 38 | 61 | 96 |\n| 1990-1995 | 166 | 84 | 65 | 46 | 15 | 10 | 35 | 47 | 91 |\n| 1995-2000 | 151 | 73 | 57 | 34 | 12 | 9 | 34 | 38 | 82 |\n| 2000-2005 | 130 | 60 | 51 | 28 | 10 | 8 | 33 | 31 | 70 |\n| 2005-2010 | 105 | 47 | 47 | 23 | 8 | 8 | 29 | 23 | 57 |\n| 2010-2015 | 84 | 37 | 45 | 20 | 6 | 7 | 26 | 19 | 46 |\n| 2015-2020 | 71 | 31 | 42 | 17 | 5 | 7 | 23 | 17 | 40 |\n| Source: United Nations | | | | | | | | | |\n\nOpen in Excel: Environmental Indicators Ireland 2021 Table 1.2 (XLS 11KB) \n\nGlobal child mortality rates, as measured by the number of deaths of children before the age of five per 1,000 live births, have fallen from an average annual 213 in 1950-1955 to 40 in 2015-2020.\n\nThe greatest relative fall in child mortality rates occurred in Europe where the average annual rate declined from 93 to 5 between 1950-1955 and 2015-2020. Europe also had the lowest average annual child mortality rate in the world in 2015-2020 at 5 deaths before the age of five per 1,000 live births.\n\nAfrica had the highest child mortality rate in the World in 2015-2020, with an average annual 71 deaths of children before age five per 1,000 live births, despite having the largest absolute fall over the 1950-2020 period.\n\n## 1.3 World: Life expectancy at birth 1950-2020\n\n 1.3 World: Life expectancy at birth 